---@class posthog.query.ExperimentExposureHealthCheck
---@field description? string|distilled.Null What the check looks for and why it matters. Missing on an answer cached before the field existed.
---@field key posthog.query.ExperimentExposureHealthCheckKey|string Stable identifier of the check.
---@field name string The problem the check looks for, as the health panel lists it.
---@field reason string|distilled.Null Why the check did not look, for the statuses not_applicable and not_checked, for example 'Runs after launch'. Null for passed and finding.
---@field rule? posthog.query.ExperimentExposureHealthCheckRule|distilled.Null How the check decides, the same for every experiment. Null for a check without a numeric rule. Missing on an answer cached before the field existed.
---@field status posthog.query.ExperimentExposureHealthCheckStatus|string passed: no problem found. finding: a finding in `health_findings`. not_applicable: the check doesn't cover the experiment's state. not_checked: an input was missing or the check failed.
---@field values? posthog.query.ExperimentExposureHealthCheckValuesMap|distilled.Null What the check read on the experiment, for every status. The suffix of a key gives the unit: _count is a count, _percentage is on the 0-100 scale, _hours is hours. A key without a suffix is a setting. Missing on an answer cached before the field existed.

---@alias posthog.query.ExperimentExposureHealthCheckKey "zero_exposures"|"srm"|"bias_risk_multiple_excluded"|"multiple_variants_share"|"test_account_filter_removes_exposures"

---@class posthog.query.ExperimentExposureHealthCheckRule
---@field minimum posthog.query.ExperimentExposureHealthRuleMinimum|distilled.Null What the check needs before it judges. Null when the check judges from the first value.
---@field test string|distilled.Null The statistical test that computes the value. Null for a count or a share.
---@field threshold number The threshold, in the unit that the suffix of the key gives.
---@field value posthog.query.ExperimentExposureHealthValueKey|string The key in `values` that the check compares with the threshold.
---@field warns posthog.query.ExperimentExposureHealthRuleSide|string above: the check reports a finding when the value is above the threshold. below: when the value is below it. A value at the threshold passes.

---@alias posthog.query.ExperimentExposureHealthCheckStatus "passed"|"finding"|"not_applicable"|"not_checked"

---@alias posthog.query.ExperimentExposureHealthCheckValuesMap { [string]: posthog.query.ExperimentExposureHealthCheckValuesValue|distilled.Null }

---@alias posthog.query.ExperimentExposureHealthCheckValuesValue string|number|boolean

---@class posthog.query.ExperimentExposureHealthFinding
---@field actions posthog.query.ExperimentExposureHealthFindingActionsList The actions that fix the problem, in order of preference.
---@field check? posthog.query.ExperimentExposureHealthCheckKey|string|distilled.Null The key of the check in `health_checks` that reported the finding. Missing on an answer cached before the field existed.
---@field code posthog.query.ExperimentExposureHealthFindingCode|string Stable identifier of the problem. Each code has one meaning across every surface that reports it.
---@field detail string What is wrong, what it does to the experiment, and how to fix it.
---@field diagnostic_ref string|distilled.Null The id of the matching diagnostic in the diagnosing-experiment-health skill, for example 'A2'. Null when the skill has none.
---@field evidence posthog.query.ExperimentExposureHealthFindingEvidenceMap The values behind the finding, such as the p-value of the sample ratio test. The keys depend on the code.
---@field reason string|distilled.Null A stable qualifier below the subcode, for example where a sample ratio mismatch is located. Null when the finding names none.
---@field severity posthog.query.ExperimentExposureHealthFindingSeverity|string How much the problem affects the results: critical, warning, or info.
---@field subcode string|distilled.Null The case within the code, when a code covers several. Null when the code has one case.
---@field title string One-line summary of the problem.

