---@class posthog.query.PathsV2Anchor
---@field item posthog.query.PathsV2Item The path item the chart anchors on. Its event must be one of the step sources.
---@field type posthog.query.PathsV2AnchorType|string `start` runs each actor's single sequence forward from the anchor item; `end` runs it up to the anchor item. Either way the anchor is the grid's single 100% node.

---@alias posthog.query.PathsV2AnchorType "start"|"end"

---@class posthog.query.PathsV2Edge
---@field anyStepCount? number|distilled.Null Unique actors who transition from source to target at any step of any of their whole journeys, the position-free count behind "went source → target at any step". Equals the two-step item-strict funnel's converted count. Only set in open mode on edges between two named items.
---@field count number Unique actors with a journey that transitions from source to target between these steps.
---@field source posthog.query.PathsV2Item|distilled.Null Source path item, or null for the source column's "other" row.
---@field stepIndex number 0-based step index of the source column; the target sits at `stepIndex + 1`.
---@field target posthog.query.PathsV2Item|distilled.Null Target path item, or null for the target column's "other" row.

---@class posthog.query.PathsV2ElementSelector
---@field anyStep? boolean|distilled.Null Match the source → target transition at any step of any whole journey instead of at one step pair: the position-free set behind an edge's anyStepCount. Requires a named source and target and open mode. Edge elements only.
---@field chain? posthog.query.PathsV2ElementSelectorChainList|distilled.Null The chain's path items in order from the anchor. Returns the actors whose anchored sequence begins with exactly these items, the set behind a hover preview's per-chain counts. Chain elements only, anchored mode only. Bounded by the step maximum: a longer chain can never match a displayed card.
---@field elementType posthog.query.PathsV2ElementType|string
---@field item? posthog.query.PathsV2Item|distilled.Null The node card's path item. Node elements only.
---@field source? posthog.query.PathsV2Item|distilled.Null The edge's source path item; omit for the source column's "other" row. Edge elements only.
---@field stepIndex? number|distilled.Null 0-based step index (column) of the element; for an edge, its source column. Required for node, other, dropOff, and positional edge elements.
---@field target? posthog.query.PathsV2Item|distilled.Null The edge's target path item; omit for the target column's "other" row. Edge elements only.

---@alias posthog.query.PathsV2ElementSelectorChainList posthog.query.PathsV2Item[]

---@alias posthog.query.PathsV2ElementType "node"|"edge"|"dropOff"|"other"|"chain"

---@class posthog.query.PathsV2Filter
---@field anchor? posthog.query.PathsV2Anchor|distilled.Null Anchor selecting anchored mode. When set, each actor contributes exactly one sequence bounded by the conversion window, so every displayed segment equals a plain funnel. Absent selects open mode, which splits an actor's events into journeys on the inactivity gap instead.
---@field applyTeamPathCleaning? boolean|distilled.Null Apply the team's path cleaning rules to naming property values before they become path items.
---@field collapseRepeats? boolean|distilled.Null Merge immediate repeats of the same path item within a journey.
---@field conversionWindowInterval? number|distilled.Null Anchored mode's single conversion window W, anchored at the anchor and reused verbatim as the emitted funnel's window. Bounds per unit are validated server-side against CONVERSION_WINDOW_INTERVAL_BOUNDS, the same funnel conversion window bounds as the gap.
---@field conversionWindowIntervalUnit? posthog.query.FunnelConversionWindowTimeUnit|string|distilled.Null
---@field excludedItems? posthog.query.PathsV2FilterExcludedItemsList|distilled.Null Path items dropped from the item universe: events deriving to one of these items are ignored as if their event were not a step source, on both the paths side and the "view as funnel" side.
---@field gapInterval? number|distilled.Null Inactivity gap that splits an actor's events into journeys. Bounds per unit are validated server-side against CONVERSION_WINDOW_INTERVAL_BOUNDS, the funnel conversion window bounds.
---@field gapIntervalUnit? posthog.query.FunnelConversionWindowTimeUnit|string|distilled.Null
---@field localPathCleaningFilters? posthog.query.PathsV2FilterLocalPathCleaningFiltersList|distilled.Null Path cleaning rules for this insight only, applied after the team's rules.
---@field maxRowsPerStep? number|distilled.Null Number of path item rows per step; items beyond this go into the "other" row.
---@field maxSteps? number|distilled.Null Number of journey steps (columns) shown.
---@field stepSources? posthog.query.PathsV2FilterStepSourcesList|distilled.Null Step sources defining which events can become path items. Defaults to the pageviews preset: `$pageview` named by `$pathname`.

---@alias posthog.query.PathsV2FilterExcludedItemsList posthog.query.PathsV2Item[]

