---@class posthog.query.TrendsFilter
---@field aggregationAxisFormat? posthog.query.AggregationAxisFormat|string|distilled.Null Y-axis value formatter. Picks a human-friendly unit per value at render time without changing the underlying series values. - `numeric` (default): raw numbers, e.g. `1,234`. - `duration`: values are in seconds; rendered as friendly units per value (`45s`, `2m 12s`, `1h 4m`). Use this whenever the series is in seconds (latency, session length, time-to-event) instead of dividing in `formula` to force minutes or hours. - `duration_ms`: values are in milliseconds; rendered as friendly units (`850ms`, `1.5s`, `1m 4s`). - `percentage`: values are already in the 0-100 range; appends `%`. - `percentage_scaled`: values are a 0-1 ratio; multiplied and rendered as `%`. - `currency`: values are in the project's base currency (set in project settings, defaults to USD); rendered with that currency symbol. For values pinned to a specific currency regardless of project base (e.g. `$ai_total_cost_usd` is always USD), use `aggregationAxisPrefix` instead. - `short`: compact notation for large counts (`1.2K`, `3.4M`).
---@field aggregationAxisPostfix? string|distilled.Null Literal suffix applied to every value (e.g. ` req`). Reserve for units that `aggregationAxisFormat` cannot express. Do not use ` mins`, ` s`, ` ms`, `%` etc. — pick the matching `aggregationAxisFormat` instead so the underlying values stay numerically correct for breakdowns, formulas, and alerts. Include any leading space yourself.
---@field aggregationAxisPrefix? string|distilled.Null Literal prefix applied to every value (e.g. `$`). Use to pin a unit or currency symbol that does not depend on `aggregationAxisFormat` — for example, when values are denominated in a fixed currency regardless of the project's base currency. Include any trailing space yourself.
---@field annotationsScope? posthog.query.AnnotationScope|string|distilled.Null Render only annotations with this scope. Unset renders every scope.
---@field breakdown_histogram_bin_count? number|distilled.Null
---@field chartStyle? posthog.query.ChartStyle|distilled.Null Chart rendering style overrides (line shape).
---@field confidenceLevel? number|distilled.Null
---@field decimalPlaces? number|distilled.Null Maximum number of decimal places shown. 1 or 2 is usually right for percentages and currency.
---@field detailedResultsAggregationType? posthog.query.DetailedResultsAggregationType|string|distilled.Null detailed results table
---@field display? posthog.query.ChartDisplayType|string|distilled.Null
---@field excludeBoxPlotOutliers? boolean|distilled.Null
---@field formula? string|distilled.Null
---@field formulaNodes? posthog.query.TrendsFilterFormulaNodesList|distilled.Null List of formulas with optional custom names. Takes precedence over formula/formulas if set.
---@field formulas? posthog.query.TrendsFilterFormulasList|distilled.Null
---@field goalLines? posthog.query.TrendsFilterGoalLinesList|distilled.Null Goal Lines
---@field hiddenLegendIndexes? posthog.query.TrendsFilterHiddenLegendIndexesList|distilled.Null
---@field hideWeekends? boolean|distilled.Null Ignored. Superseded by `dateRange.daysOfWeek`, which excludes the days from the query instead of only hiding their buckets. Still accepted so existing API clients keep working.
---@field legendPosition? posthog.query.LegendPosition|string|distilled.Null Where the in-chart legend sits relative to the plot. Only applies to the in-chart legend.
---@field metricChangeDecreaseColor? string|distilled.Null Metric display: change pill color when the metric decreased. Defaults to red.
---@field metricChangeIncreaseColor? string|distilled.Null Metric display: change pill color when the metric increased. Defaults to green.
---@field metricColorByDirection? boolean|distilled.Null Metric display: color the sparkline by whether the metric increased or decreased.
---@field metricLineDecreaseColor? string|distilled.Null Metric display: line color when the metric decreased. Defaults to red.
---@field metricLineIncreaseColor? string|distilled.Null Metric display: line color when the metric increased. Defaults to green.
---@field metricShowChange? boolean|distilled.Null Show the period-over-period change pill on the Metric display.
---@field metricSummary? posthog.query.MetricSummary|string|distilled.Null Metric display: which summary the resting headline shows — the period total, the average, or the latest point. Hovering the sparkline always shows the hovered point's value. Also drives the change pill: total/average compare against the previous period when "compare to previous" is on; latest compares first→last of the series.
